{
  "name": "dimetrodon",
  "_about": "SCULPTED (2026-11-08, tools/creaturegen/prehistoric/dimetrodon.py): DIMETRODON GRANDIS, an early Permian sphenacodontid SYNAPSID (not a dinosaur: on the line to the mammals), 3.2 m long, sprawling. The SAIL: one `fin` sheet in the midplane rooted along the back from the neck's root to the hips, its rim the exact outline over 19 neural spines -- low over the shoulders, highest (.9 m over the back) at mid-back, falling to the sacrum, a semicircular arc -- sagging a little between the spine tips (scalloped); thin (12 mm, a sharp rim), faired into the back; each spine a thin `horn` rising from inside the back THROUGH the sheet to just past its rim, standing out of both faces as a rib; the back's tone at its base, an ochre band up the middle, a dark rim. A deep narrow skull with a tall snout, the upper jaw margin STEPPED (a notch between premaxilla and maxilla for the lower jaw's big front teeth), the maxilla bowed down at the canines; differentiated teeth (horns): two premaxillary incisors, two great canine fangs each side, small cheek teeth; the lower front tusk and its row. The temporal opening a shallow hollow behind the eye. A deep rigid barrel trunk (the sail spans it: no trunk swing), sprawled legs with five clawed toes (claws horns, the 4th toe longest), a long tapering tail swinging as it walks. Muted olive-brown, scaly, dark bars across the back fading down the flanks and rings down the tail (paints: a coat recolours them), the belly and jaw pale. Coats: olive (the sail ochre-banded), rust, slate; variant `juvenile` (.4).",
